      "side": 1,
      "message": "`aff \u0026 ~(GENMASK_ULL(32, 8) \u003e\u003e (lpi_aff \u003c\u003c 3))` uses a 25-bit `GENMASK(32,8)` where the Aff granularity boundaries are byte-aligned; for CommonLPIAff\u003d\u003d1 it yields Aff bits [31:25] rather than [31:24], dropping the low bit of each affinity level. Per the spec, the group key should be the full Aff3 / Aff3.Aff2 / Aff3.Aff2.Aff1 prefix. This mis-scopes the \"same property table\" grouping in `handle_lpi_enable`/`disable` and can wrongly reject a legal PROPBASER. Could you re-derive the mask against the CommonLPIAff encoding?",
